                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">“Medicinal Chemistry” is an important specialized core course for undergraduate students of pharmacy. By means of the study of this course, students should understand major theory of Medicinal Chemsitry (such as Receptor theory, Metabolic Antagonism, Enzyme inhibitor, Pharmacophore Modeling, SAR/QSAR, Me-too drugs, Prodrug, Chiral drugs, Bioisosterism). Important typical drugs are also introduced according to their chemical structures and therapeutic activities.&nbsp;</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
